summary:
  The mark survives a bridge restart even when it is ahead of the clock, so
  after the clock is set back every media key is dropped until it catches up.

history:
  The mark is kept across a restart so an obeyed key is never obeyed again,
  and a fresh daemon's first number is the clock. When the clock has gone
  back in between (a dual-boot machine whose clock is corrected after login
  goes back by the whole timezone), every new number sits below the mark and
  the keys stay dead for as long as the clock went back, hours in that case.
  That is the silent drop ef3be71 was written to end.

target:
  package/contents/ui/MprisCommandGate.qml

find:
          if (lastSeq > nowMs)

replace:
          if (false)

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_mpriscommandgate.qml::test_a_clock_set_back_cannot_deafen_the_next_bridge.
  Line-neutral.
